From e97b0a68e836e3e2e444d318f16e29a4cde62ad2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christoph Engelbert (noctarius)" <chris@simplyblock.io>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 16:27:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nfsd: ask clients to retry a file handle of an export not
 back yet

After a server restart, nfsd starts and its grace period begins before
whatever exports its filesystems has exported all of them again.
Clients reconnect and reclaim at once, and a reclaim naming a file on an
export not yet back is answered NFS4ERR_STALE. The client then drops the
reclaimed open for good, and the application's I/O on it fails with
EBADF.

Seen on a restarted server: one client reclaimed at 11.8s, the export
its two open files were on came back at 12.7s, and both opens were lost
with "state recovery failed for open file ..., error = -116".

During grace, answer an unknown export with NFS4ERR_DELAY, which
clients retry. Once grace has ended, an unknown export is stale as
before.
---
 fs/nfsd/nfsfh.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/fs/nfsd/nfsfh.c b/fs/nfsd/nfsfh.c
index 3ab4b1b..eab8d2c 100644
--- a/fs/nfsd/nfsfh.c
+++ b/fs/nfsd/nfsfh.c
@@ -197,8 +197,16 @@ static __be32 nfsd_set_fh_dentry(struct svc_rqst *rqstp, struct net *net,
 	if (IS_ERR(exp)) {
 		trace_nfsd_set_fh_dentry_badexport(rqstp, fhp, PTR_ERR(exp));
 
+		/*
+		 * During grace an export a client still holds state on may
+		 * not have been exported again yet: the server restarted, and
+		 * whatever exports its filesystems is still at it. STALE ends
+		 * that state for good (the client drops a reclaimed open and
+		 * fails the application's I/O with EBADF), so ask the client
+		 * to retry. Once grace is over, an unknown export is stale.
+		 */
 		if (PTR_ERR(exp) == -ENOENT)
-			return error;
+			return locks_in_grace(net) ? nfserr_jukebox : error;
 
 		return nfserrno(PTR_ERR(exp));
 	}
